## Going-forward rule: structural fix preferred when bug class can recur (set 2026-05-09)

**When facing a bug whose ROOT CAUSE is "same pattern at multiple sites
drifted apart" (Class 18 mirror, parallel paths), prefer compile-time
enforcement (X-macro registry, helper extraction with all callers
unified) over direct patch — even if direct patch is cheaper today.**

**Why:** v5.9.5b production-caller class recurred 4× before
STAMP_CFG_AUTOPOPULATE extinguished it (v5.14.1). PARITY-009/010/011/012
were 9 sub-gaps of the same Class 18 shape at function-composition level;
PostLoadSetup registries closed all 9 in one ship (v5.14.2.E.1).

**How to apply:** when `/parity-check` or `/merge-scan` surfaces
duplication or mirror gaps, ask: "would a registry / helper extraction +
compile-time enforcement prevent the next instance?" If yes, that's the
v5.X ship shape. Direct patches are for true one-off bugs only.

**Caramel's framing 2026-05-09:** "headache now > issues later. set it
up to be easy to maintain going forward, even if it does add more work
now." Validated 4/4 times this session (10-param helper → X-macro
refactor; Option F → Option D revised; Option 2 → Option 3; bash CLI
catch-up → C++ wrapper binary deferral).

This rule applies to Claude AND Gemini sessions; same shape as
boundary-stable refactor preference (2026-05-06).

Codified in:
- `CLAUDE.md` item 19 (public; references this without naming Caramel)
- `DOCS/RECURRING_BUG_PATTERNS.md` Class 18 (strengthened sub-clause)
- `DOCS/TECH_DEBT.md` (auto-write contract; this file)
- `/readiness` Check 24 (mirror-function audit) + Check 25 (TECH_DEBT scan)
- `/trace-deps` Step 6 strengthening (call-sequence enumeration)

## Going-forward rule: deferred items must be queryable, not buried (set 2026-05-09)

**Any architectural item that's deferred from current ship MUST land in
`DOCS/TECH_DEBT.md` ledger** with: what + why deferred + cost estimate +
trigger + cross-ref. Don't bury in code comments / postmortems / chat
memory — those get forgotten.

**Why:** Caramel's pushback 2026-05-09: "what if I forget about that
stuff, like doesn't addressing the deferred items now make future
maintenance easier?" Answer: address now if architecturally bounded;
defer if separate concern. But deferred items hidden anywhere except
the ledger are invisible to future ships.

**How to apply:** same auto-write contract as PARITY_ISSUES.md. When
`/readiness` Check 25, `/merge-scan`, or any audit identifies a
deferral candidate, agent MUST add the entry. `/readiness` Check 25
scans the ledger at every ship and surfaces entries whose surface area
overlaps with the ship's files-touched. Operator reviews at ship
boundary; agent does mechanical bookkeeping.

Established 2026-05-09 alongside the structural-fix-preferred rule
above. TECH_DEBT.md initial 6 entries cover bash CLI catch-up,
centralized engine removal, parser refactor, dual-tau naming,
strict-mode unification, FOREACH_STAMP_BOUND_MODEL_CONST refactor.

## Going-forward rule for parity audits (set 2026-05-09)

**Any time `/parity-check` (or any audit that surfaces a parity
issue) finds a new finding, the agent MUST auto-write the entry
into `DOCS/PARITY_ISSUES.md` (workspace-private, symlinked into
engine repo).** Don't defer to "operator copies after review" —
the ledger is the single source of truth. A finding that exists
only in a transient audit report but not in the ledger is invisible
to future audits and gets re-discovered noise.

Same auto-write applies to status updates: when a verification
rerun confirms FIXED, NOT-A-BUG, or recategorization, the agent
updates the ledger entry directly. Operator reviews at sprint
boundaries to recategorize / accept / reject; agent does the
mechanical bookkeeping.

The /parity-check skill spec encodes the auto-write contract +
cross-reference-before-flagging discipline. This CLAUDE.local.md
entry exists to make the rule visible across all skills/audits
that touch parity surfaces, not just /parity-check.

Established 2026-05-09 after the v5.14.1.B series ships closed
PARITY-001 through PARITY-005. PARITY_ISSUES.md created same day
as the running ledger; this rule formalizes its operational role.

