## Going-forward rule: cohort-audit when new cfg field has siblings (set 2026-05-11; pre-implementation draft)

**When adding a new boolean cfg field that has 2+ siblings in the same
semantic family (e.g., `ridge_*`, `confidence_*`, `bandit_*`), run the
5-criteria `DESIGN_SPECS/cfg-flag-eligibility-criteria.md` framework
on the COHORT, not just the new field.**

**Three outcomes:**
- **All eligible** → migrate the cohort in the same ship (intra-family
  consistency; prevents partial-migration tech-debt class)
- **Mixed eligibility** → migrate the eligible subset + auto-write
  TECH_DEBT entry for ineligible siblings explaining per-sibling
  rejection rationale
- **None eligible** → document the family-wide rejection rationale in
  TECH_DEBT; new field stays direct alongside siblings

**Why:** v5.14.9.F.2 / v5.14.10.B migration sweeps left `ridge_within_horizon`,
`ridge_across_horizons`, `exit_blender_mode` as direct int cfg fields
while migrating other ML flags. Intra-family inconsistency surfaced
2026-05-11 during v5.14.11 audit synthesis — Decision 4 corrected by
cohort-migrating all 4 ridge_* fields. Without this rule, similar
oversights accumulate per-sprint into a tech-debt class.

**How to apply:** at plan-synthesis time, when a new boolean cfg field
appears in proposed scope, grep for sibling fields in the same domain
(e.g., `*_enabled` / `*_mode` / `ridge_*` in ML domain). If 2+ siblings
exist, cohort-audit is part of plan-readiness check (per CLAUDE.md item 13
reuse-audit + item 16). Lives alongside `/readiness` Check 24 (mirror-
function audit) + Check 25 (TECH_DEBT scan).

**Caramel's framing 2026-05-11:** "id rather not add tech debt" — captured
at v5.14.11 plan-synthesis after seeing that (1) intra-family inconsistency
would itself be a tech-debt class and (2) the framework verdict + codebase
precedent diverged. Pre-implementation draft; refine as v5.14.11 ships
and the cohort migration validates the discipline.

Codified in:
- `DESIGN_SPECS/cfg-flag-eligibility-criteria.md` (new "Cohort audit when
  new field has siblings" section; v5.14.11 ridge_* as canonical example)
- `CLAUDE.md` item 13 (X-macro registry; reuse-audit cross-ref)
- This file (auto-write contract for cohort-audit findings)

## Going-forward rule: FEATURE_LOOKUP.md auto-write on operator-visible features (set 2026-05-12)

**Any time a new operator-visible feature ships — new cfg flag,
new ML mechanism, new persistence file, new GUI surface, new
boot gate, new strategy / regime / blender variant — the agent
MUST add an entry to `tick-trader-percore-workspace/FEATURE_LOOKUP.md`.**
Sister auto-write to `DOCS/PARITY_ISSUES.md` (parity findings)
and `DOCS/TECH_DEBT.md` (deferred items).

**What counts as "operator-visible":**
- New cfg flag the operator might toggle (not internal-only)
- New observability surface (panel field, log line, halt_reason code)
- New persistence file (`*_state.json`, model bundle layout change)
- New boot gate or refusal mode (live-mode strict, readiness check)
- New training pipeline knob (CSV input, side selector, label kind)
- New fallback path (e.g., "if no models, use legacy TP/SL")

**What does NOT count (skip the auto-write):**
- Pure refactors that don't change operator behavior
- Internal helper extraction (X-macro splits, AUTOPOPULATE companions)
- Bug fixes that restore expected behavior (don't entry-document
  what was always supposed to work)
- Performance optimizations bytewise-identical to prior path

**Entry format** (one block per feature, ~40-80 LOC):
- `### <feature_name> (vX.Y.Z+)`
- `**What:**` 1-sentence summary
- `**Cfg flags:**` list
- `**Fallback:**` what happens when disabled / inputs missing
- `**Where to verify:**` GUI panel field / log line / file (with file:line refs)
- `**Paper-test sanity:**` numbered steps to confirm working in paper
- `**Gotchas:**` known parity / interaction concerns
- `**Related:**` related features + persistence files

**Why:** Caramel's question 2026-05-12 — "how will I know if the
bandit and multi-model configs actually work?" — surfaced that
the X-macro registries give the FIELD NAMES + tooltips give the
LOCAL BEHAVIOR but nowhere documents "to verify this feature, look
at THIS surface in THIS panel and run THIS sanity loop." Doc bridges
that gap.

**How to apply:** at sprint-close / sub-ship close, if a new
operator-visible feature shipped, agent updates FEATURE_LOOKUP.md
before declaring complete. Operator reviews at boundary; agent
does mechanical bookkeeping.

Codified in:
- `tick-trader-percore-workspace/FEATURE_LOOKUP.md` (the doc itself;
  seeded 2026-05-12 with 20 features at v5.15.4 close)
- This file (auto-write contract)
- `/ship` skill (post-coding ritual) gets a FEATURE_LOOKUP check
  added to its verification gate
- `/sync-workspace` already mirrors workspace root MDs

