## Going-forward rule: decoupling-endgoal positioning at each fix (set 2026-05-12)

**When making changes that touch GUI ↔ runtime interfaces**
(foxml_suite GUI ↔ training entry points; engine ↔ engine_gui display;
TUISnapshot publication; any state-flow across the GUI-process
boundary; CLI mode dispatch; cfg ownership across viewer/runtime;
logging path discipline), **document the decoupling implication in
`plans/_future/2026-05-12-decoupling-endgoal-roadmap.md`** (workspace-
private). Establish patterns that POSITION us for separation rather
than fight it. The cumulative breadcrumbs become the pseudo-plan for
the eventual Grafana-style decoupling sprint.

**Three outcomes per ship:**
- **Positive positioning** → write breadcrumb describing how the
  change makes future decoupling easier (X-macro registry exposed via
  cmdline, mmap-friendly bit-packed flags, atomic publication
  discipline, table-driven gates, disk-based state externalization,
  etc.). Update readiness checklist if applicable.
- **Anti-breadcrumb** → change CONFLICTS with decoupling (callback
  registry with fn pointers, in-process-only state, mutex protecting
  cross-thread state where seqlock would work). Redirect the design
  at fix time; document the redirect in the anti-breadcrumb section.
- **Neutral** → change doesn't touch the decoupling surface; no entry
  needed.

**Why:** Caramel framing 2026-05-12 —
> *"as we progress fixes should lay out the approach to actually
> decouple it since we have the context in memory, that way when we
> actually go to decouple, we basically already have a psuedo plan
> laid out."*

By the time the decoupling sprint kicks off (post-v5.15 paper-test
era; sequenced with `plans/_future/2026-05-08-v6.0-CANDIDATE-headless-service-colo.md`),
the doc IS the pseudo-plan: endgoal named + breadcrumbs accumulated +
open design questions surfaced + readiness checklist saying "yes we
can proceed cleanly."

**How to apply:** at plan-synthesis time for any ship touching the
relevant surfaces, the sub-plan's verification gate gets a "decoupling
roadmap entry written" checkbox. At sub-ship close, the breadcrumb
gets written before the umbrella tag lands.

**Pre-seeded with retroactive entries** for v5.15.0 through v5.15.4
in the roadmap doc (these were the first ships writing breadcrumbs;
the doc was opened at v5.15 sprint planning 2026-05-12).

Codified in:
- `plans/_future/2026-05-12-decoupling-endgoal-roadmap.md` (the living
  doc itself; sections: endgoal architecture, decoupling axes, running
  breadcrumbs, readiness checklist, open design questions,
  anti-breadcrumbs)
- This file (auto-write contract for breadcrumbs at every relevant
  ship)
- Each v5.15.X sub-plan verification gate includes "decoupling roadmap
  entry written"
- Companion: `plans/_future/2026-05-08-v6.0-CANDIDATE-headless-service-colo.md`
  (engine-side decoupling architecture; the roadmap doc extends this
  to the suite side + adds the running breadcrumbs discipline)
